  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Iron Bow Technologies reported $297M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Iron Bow Technologies received 397 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $749K, and obligations are down 37.1% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $238M, followed by the Department of Transportation at $58.5M. Other federal buyers with smaller obligations include the Smithsonian Institution, Equal Employment Opportunity Commission, and Department of Veterans Affairs. Iron Bow Technologies is concentrated in a few markets: Other Computer Related Services ($120M), Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing ($101M), and Electronic Computer Manufacturing ($72.2M). Software Publishers appear among the top markets at $2.6M and $131K in two entries. Yearly obligations rose from $513M in FY21 to a peak of $706M in FY24, then declined to $472M in FY25 and to $297M in FY26 to date. The present-year totals are partial fiscal-year figures and reflect contract obligations rather than total contract values.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change versus prior years?",
        "body": "Fiscal-year obligations rose from $513M in FY21 to $706M in FY24, then fell to $472M in FY25. FY26 to date obligations are $297M, and obligations are down 37.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest federal buyers of Iron Bow Technologies?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $238M and is the largest buyer. The Department of Transportation obligated $58.5M, and smaller buyers include the Smithsonian Institution ($601K), Equal Employment Opportunity Commission ($436K), and Department of Veterans Affairs ($426K)."
      }
    ]
  },
